WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.373
Public Forum is a two versus two debate.

00:00:02.373 --> 00:00:05.815
One team supports the resolution and the other opposes it.

00:00:05.815 --> 00:00:08.960
Speaking first does not automatically mean being pro.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:13.113
The coin flip process determines choices about side or speaking order.

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:16.080
Confirm the tournament rules before a competition.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:22.818
The standard practice sequence starts with four minute constructives, followed by
crossfire.

00:00:22.818 --> 00:00:26.730
Second speakers give four minute rebuttals and another crossfire.

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:29.318
First speakers give three minute summaries.

00:00:29.318 --> 00:00:33.652
After grand crossfire, second speakers deliver two minute final focuses.

00:00:33.652 --> 00:00:35.759
Each crossfire lasts three minutes.

00:00:35.759 --> 00:00:39.310
This app starts with three minutes of preparation per team.

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:44.121
Use crossfire to ask short questions and listen to the answer.

00:00:44.121 --> 00:00:48.606
In summary, choose the arguments that still matter and explain their impacts.

00:00:48.606 --> 00:00:51.868
In final focus, tell the judge why your comparison wins.

00:00:51.868 --> 00:00:56.178
Do not rely on a concession unless you explain its importance in a speech.

00:00:56.178 --> 00:00:58.915
Try the complete sequence in the practice room.
